\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge links and scalar orbit weights}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{In the [global orbit weight](fdip-00ZW), one rotation acts on every
vertex. Suppose instead that two neighboring vertices can be rotated
independently. An edge can carry a link that transports one
value to the other endpoint. When both fields and links vary, which
weights survive independent changes at the vertices?}

